  clock: 2  # ebcd
  nonce: ebcd  # ebcd
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 134a06d505): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES.\n\nRepro (fixture: index.html with `<script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.ts\">` and `<script src=\"./src/util.js\">`; src/main.ts and src/util.js exist; surveyed from /tmp): both script tags give an edge html:index.html:1-1:file:file -> `javascript:/src/main.ts:0-0:ref:external_symbol` / `javascript:./src/util.js:0-0:ref:external_symbol`; each dst node is kind=external_symbol, language=javascript, path=<external>, supply_chain tier 3 external_dep (\"unresolved external reference\"). The real nodes typescript:src/main.ts:1-1:file:file and javascript:src/util.js:1-1:file:file exist in the same output. The entrypoints list carries `script_module` for typescript:src/main.ts:1-1:file:file, so the two-surfaces disagreement holds.\n\nCode: html.py:154 `script_ref_id = f\"javascript:{script_src}:0-0:ref:script\"` -- raw URL, no resolution, language hardcoded.\n\nDrift:\n- Edge type is no longer `script_src`: 730a297975 (2026-06-25, INV-vavat) made it edge_type=references with meta.ref_construct=\"script_src\" (html.py:160-170). Title/description wording \"script_src edge\" should say \"references edge (ref_construct=script_src)\".\n- The dst id's kind slot serializes as `ref:external_symbol` (the analyzer still writes `ref:script`).\n- Wider than the row says: a RELATIVE src (`./src/util.js`) of an existing in-repo file is also unresolved, not only the root-absolute `/src/main.ts` form. The fix needs both: relative -> against the html file's directory; leading \"/\" -> against the web root (the html file's dir / repo root for Vite).\n- The \"phantom\" also mislabels language: a .ts target gets language=javascript (same family as WI-komum's hardcode).\nINV-vavat (cross-ref) is satisfied; nothing supersedes this row."  # ebcd
